WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.275
Hi, I'm Rafter!

00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:06.213
Today: how the sandbox behind Claude Code's shell keeps a command from

00:00:06.213 --> 00:00:08.838
your files and the internet, with no container.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.334
Mounts decide which files a command can see or change.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:17.212
Its only network is a socket to a proxy that checks every host.

00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:25.221
Without a sandbox, the agent asks before each command, and people stop reading.

00:00:25.641 --> 00:00:29.180
With one, the boundary is drawn once, and only a new host asks.

00:00:31.192 --> 00:00:34.433
On Linux, the policy becomes one bubblewrap command line.

00:00:34.853 --> 00:00:37.012
First, the whole disk is mounted read-only.

00:00:37.784 --> 00:00:40.209
Then the project folder is bound back, writable.

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:43.784
Shell startup files and git hooks are frozen again on top.

00:00:44.204 --> 00:00:47.702
A denied folder gets an empty mount over it, so its files are gone.

00:00:48.122 --> 00:00:49.655
And the network is removed.

00:00:49.655 --> 00:00:50.881
Only loopback is left.

00:00:52.675 --> 00:00:56.823
The command's proxy variables point at a small relay inside the sandbox.

00:00:57.243 --> 00:01:01.306
The relay forwards into a Unix socket, the only thing that crosses the wall.

00:01:01.726 --> 00:01:05.020
On the host, a proxy checks the hostname against the allowlist.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.952
An allowed host gets through.

00:01:06.952 --> 00:01:10.277
Anything else gets a four oh three, logged against the command.

00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:16.401
In Claude Code, writes outside the project and denied hosts fail inside the sandbox.

00:01:16.821 --> 00:01:21.073
Its proxies allow known hosts, deny listed ones, and ask you about the rest.

00:01:22.425 --> 00:01:25.775
On my Linux machine, a wrapped command cost about a tenth of

00:01:25.775 --> 00:01:27.450
a second with the proxy up.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.963
The full command line tool, most of a second.

00:01:31.142 --> 00:01:33.347
An allowed domain is a whole domain.

00:01:33.347 --> 00:01:35.867
The proxy reads hostnames, not what you send.

00:01:38.692 --> 00:01:41.957
Mounts for files, one socket for the network, and a proxy

00:01:41.957 --> 00:01:43.145
that checks every host.

00:01:43.565 --> 00:01:45.631
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:45.631 --> 00:01:46.221
I'm Rafter.

00:01:46.221 --> 00:01:46.516
Bye!
